{"id":"bezer","name":"Bezer","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:bezer"],"types":[{"type":"place","from":"places atlas"},{"type":"person","from":"UBS: Names of People"}],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Bezer","text":"Ore of gold or silver. (1.) A city of the Reubenites; one of the three cities of refuge on the east of Jordan (Deut. 4: 43; Josh. 20:8). It has been identified with the modern ruined village of Burazin, some 12 miles north of Heshbon; also with Kasur-el-Besheir, 2 miles south-west of Dibon. (2.) A descendant of Asher (1 Chr. 7:37)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1221","lemma":"בֶּצֶר","xlit":"Betser","gloss":"Betser, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Bezer","count":5,"share":1},{"strong":"H4057","lemma":"מִדְבָּר","xlit":"midbâr","gloss":"a pasture","kjv":"desert, south, speech, wilderness","count":3,"share":0.6}],"verses":["Deut.4.43","Josh.20.8","Josh.21.36","1Chr.6.78","1Chr.7.37"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"desert","type":"lexical","strong":"H4057","why":"both lead with מִדְבָּר (H4057)"},{"id":"deserts","type":"lexical","strong":"H4057","why":"both lead with מִדְבָּר (H4057)"},{"id":"paran","type":"lexical","strong":"H4057","why":"both lead with מִדְבָּר (H4057)"},{"id":"zin","type":"lexical","strong":"H4057","why":"both lead with מִדְבָּר (H4057)"},{"id":"ziph","type":"lexical","strong":"H4057","why":"both lead with מִדְבָּר (H4057)"}],"works":[{"work":"antiquities","title":"Antiquities of the Jews","count":1,"chapters":[{"chapter":"AntIV.7","count":1,"book":"Ant. 4","title":"How The Hebrews Fought With The Midianites, And Overcame Them."}]}]}
